@startuml ai-sdlc-flow
title ai-sdlc — outer delivery loop, exact behaviours
skinparam ConditionEndStyle hline
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left
skinparam wrapWidth 260

|#F5F5F5|Human|
|#EAF3FF|Agent|
|#FFF3E0|Deterministic|

|Human|
start
:/plugin marketplace add rubicarbon/ai-sdlc
/plugin install ai-sdlc@ai-sdlc-kit
/plugin install mattpocock-skills;
:/ai-sdlc:sdlc-init;

|Deterministic|
:scripts/init/detect.sh
platform from git remote, CLI presence + login,
stack, verify-command candidates,
mattpocock-skills installed?;

|Agent|
:ask only what detection could not settle
platform / tier / team.mode /
commands.verify|format|lint /
environments / cost caps (tier 3);

|Deterministic|
if (sdlc.config.json present and project finished?) then (yes)
  :report "already-initialised";
  stop
else (no)
endif
:validate answers against sdlc.config.schema.json (jq only)
write sdlc.config.json;
:scripts/init/run.sh --tier N — rendering is cumulative
double-brace MARKER substitution only, render.sh refuses
any unresolved marker, every file recorded by hash in
.sdlc/managed-files.json (upgrade can tell an unchanged
file from a changed template from a user edit,
user-edited files never overwritten without --force);
:tier 0 Foundation
CLAUDE.md managed block (or AGENTS.md), CONTEXT.md seed,
docs/agents/domain.md, .claude/settings.json deny rules (merged,
never clobbered), .gitignore markers;
:tier 1 Artifacts
REVIEW.md, docs/agents/issue-tracker.md (github|azure),
.sdlc/ tree, docs/adr/;
:tier 2 Review policy
no new files — next_steps: sdlc-platform branch_protect_apply <default-branch>;
:tier 3 Automation
CI templates (.github/workflows/sdlc-*.yml |
.azuredevops/pipelines/sdlc-*.yml), PR template,
CODEOWNERS (GitHub) / azure.requiredReviewers, cost caps,
next_steps: sdlc-platform ci_workflow_install;
note right
  sdlc.config.json now exists =>
  all four hooks become active.
  Tiers never turn hooks on or off.
end note

|Human|
:/ai-sdlc:sdlc-metrics-baseline — at tier 0
baseline.sh refuses once tier 1 artifacts exist
(--force overrides and records that fact);

|Agent|
repeat
:ai-sdlc:sdlc-loop  /  /ai-sdlc:sdlc-status
names the next stage from artifacts, never from memory;
|Deterministic|
:scripts/loop/precondition.sh <spec|tickets|build|verify|ship>
exit 0 = may start
exit 2 = missing artifact + the command that produces it
exit 1 = error;

|Agent|
:1. Frame — /ai-sdlc:sdlc-start <one line>
calls mattpocock-skills:grilling + domain-modeling
commits CONTEXT.md terms, docs/adr/*;

|Human|
:2. Spec — type /mattpocock-skills:to-spec
user-invoked upstream skill: the agent can only tell you
what to type => <feature>/spec.md;
:3. Tickets — type /mattpocock-skills:to-tickets
=> issues/NN-*.md with "Blocked by:" edges
and "Status: ready-for-agent";

|Agent|
if (platform == none?) then (yes)
else (github | azure)
  :4. Publish — /ai-sdlc:sdlc-publish <feature-dir>
  scripts/publish/publish.sh via sdlc-platform
  work_item_create / work_item_link / work_item_comment
  tracker ids written back as first-line markers
  + publish-manifest.json;
endif

|Deterministic|
:precondition.sh build requires
a feature dir, >=1 issues/NN-*.md,
>=1 ticket "Status: ready-for-agent",
publish-manifest.json when platform != none;

|Human|
:5. Build — branch named for the ticket,
type /mattpocock-skills:implement (drives tdd);
|Agent|
:run commands.format, commands.lint, commands.verify
before finishing — the agent's job after a coherent change,
not a per-edit hook, commits reference the ticket id;
:6. Review — mattpocock-skills:code-review
review notes on the PR or ticket;

|Human|
:7. /ai-sdlc:sdlc-verify [--security];
|Agent|
:spawn sdlc-verifier in a fresh context
tools: Read, Grep, Glob, Bash — model: inherit
guard-verifier-readonly denies its file edits;
|Deterministic|
if (git status --porcelain clean?) then (clean)
  :run commands.verify on HEAD
  write "**Tree:** clean";
else (dirty)
  :scripts/verify/run-isolated.sh
  detached worktree of HEAD (or --ref) under <artifacts>/tmp/,
  commands.verifySetup then commands.verify inside it,
  worktree removed, fingerprint of the main checkout compared
  before/after (HEAD, git ls-files -s, git diff HEAD,
  hash of every untracked non-ignored file)
  exit 0 pass | 1 fail | 2 usage/env | 4 main checkout changed
  write "**Tree:** isolated" — or stop and ask for a commit;
endif
:report stored verbatim as .sdlc/verify/<date>-<sha>.md
exactly one **Verdict:**, one **Commit:** == HEAD, one **Tree:**
PASS requires every acceptance criterion Pass with observable
evidence (test name + output line, or file:line) and exit 0;
note right
  A single "Not verified" = FAIL.
  scripts/loop/_reports.sh rejects a PASS
  without exactly one valid Tree line, so a
  working-tree run is never release evidence.
end note

|Agent|
:8. Security — sdlc-security-auditor over the diff,
sdlc-security-review check list per changed file,
ranked per REVIEW.md => .sdlc/verify/<date>-<sha>-security.md;
:9. PR — sdlc-platform pr_create;
|Human|
:a human code owner approves
(CI agent review comments only — never approves,
never requests changes, branch protection requires
code-owner review, review.requiredApprovals,
stale-review dismissal, no force pushes);

:10. /ai-sdlc:sdlc-ship <pr-id> [--version <tag>];
|Deterministic|
:scripts/ship/preflight.sh --pr <id> — read-only, exit 0 = all green
gate 1 newest verify report bound to HEAD is a valid PASS
gate 2 newest *-security.md parses and Blocking == 0
gate 3 working tree clean
gate 4 pr_get review_decision == approved
gate 5 pr_checks exit 0
gate 6 .sdlc/release/AUTHORIZED-<HEAD sha> valid;
if (ready?) then (false)
  |Agent|
  :print every gate with ok:false plus its evidence and the
  command that fixes it, then stop — gate 6 is expected to
  fail on the first run;
  |Human|
  :run at your OWN terminal:
  scripts/ship/authorize.sh --sha <HEAD sha> --ttl-minutes 120
  refuses to run when CLAUDECODE, CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT
  or CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR is set;
  |Deterministic|
  :marker validated by scripts/ship/_authz.sh —
  authorised_by=, authorised_at=, expires= (digits, strictly
  in the future), commit= (full sha == HEAD == file name),
  each exactly once, same validator backs gate 6 and the
  gate-production hook, so they cannot disagree;
  |Agent|
  :re-run preflight, continue only when ready is true;
else (true)
endif
:render .sdlc/releases/<version>.md from
templates/artifacts/release.md.tmpl, one --var per marker,
rollback rehearsal walked with the human,
"not rehearsed" written when it was not performed,
never invented;
:run commands.deployProduction with
SDLC_ENVIRONMENT=production and SDLC_SHA=<HEAD sha> exported
(key unset => stop and ask the human, never guess);
|Deterministic|
:gate-production allows it — marker complete, bound to HEAD,
unexpired, platform side adds its own human gate
(GitHub production environment reviewers / Azure Approvals);
|Agent|
:update RELEASE_AUTHORISED_BY and RELEASE_WATCH,
tell the user to commit the release note and tag the release;

|Human|
:11. Learn — /ai-sdlc:sdlc-postmortem,
/ai-sdlc:sdlc-metrics-report;
|Deterministic|
:scripts/metrics/collect.sh via sdlc-platform metrics_export,
scripts/metrics/report.py renders the four DORA keys plus
counterweights (revert rate, PR size, review latency, code churn,
defect escape rate, cost per merged PR from scripts/cost/report.sh)
with the sample size next to every number
(on Azure, PR size is null unless computed from local git);
|Agent|
repeat while (another ticket or feature?) is (yes) not (no)
stop
@enduml
